---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
---

<Layout title="Home">
  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="py-16 sm:py-24 text-center">
    <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-indigo-500 dark:text-indigo-400 mb-4">
      NeurIPS 2026 Workshop
    </p>
    <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-gray-900 dark:text-white leading-tight max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      Foundations of LLM Post-Training<br class="hidden sm:block" /> in Changing Environments
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-indigo-600 dark:text-indigo-400 font-medium">
      <a href="https://neurips.cc" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="hover:underline">NeurIPS</a> 2026 &middot; Paris, France
    </p>
    <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-3">
      <a href={`${base}/call/`} class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 rounded-lg bg-indigo-600 hover:bg-indigo-700 text-white px-5 py-2.5 text-sm font-semibold transition-colors shadow-sm">
        Call for Papers &rarr;
      </a>
      <a href={`${base}/speakers/`} class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 rounded-lg border border-gray-300 dark:border-gray-700 hover:bg-gray-50 dark:hover:bg-gray-900 px-5 py-2.5 text-sm font-semibold text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 transition-colors">
        Invited Speakers
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Title image -->
  <div class="mb-16 rounded-2xl overflow-hidden shadow-md">
    <img
      src={`${base}/images/other/test_img.JPG`}
      alt="Workshop banner"
      class="w-full object-cover max-h-72"
    />
  </div>

  <!-- Partners -->
  <section class="mb-16">
    <p class="text-center text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-gray-400 dark:text-gray-500 mb-6">In Partnership With</p>
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-center gap-10">
      <a href="https://warwick.ac.uk" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
        <img
          src={`${base}/images/uni%20logos/University_of_Warwick/University_of_Warwick_idvrMZjjfH_1.png`}
          alt="University of Warwick"
          class="h-10 object-contain dark:invert"
        />
      </a>
      <div class="h-10 w-px bg-gray-200 dark:bg-gray-700"></div>
      <a href="https://www.ox.ac.uk" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
        <img
          src={`${base}/images/uni%20logos/oxford/Oxford%20rectangle%20Logo%20RGB%20DIGITAL/rectangle%20RGB.png`}
          alt="University of Oxford"
          class="h-[68px] object-contain"
        />
      </a>
      <div class="h-10 w-px bg-gray-200 dark:bg-gray-700"></div>
      <a href="https://www.ellis.ox.ac.uk/home" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
        <img
          src={`${base}/images/ellis_logos/ellis-logo_horizontal_black_2023-OXFORD.png`}
          alt="Ellison Institute of Technology Oxford"
          class="block dark:hidden h-10 object-contain"
        />
        <img
          src={`${base}/images/ellis_logos/ellis-logo_horizontal_white_2023-OXFORD.png`}
          alt="Ellison Institute of Technology Oxford"
          class="hidden dark:block h-10 object-contain"
        />
      </a>
      <div class="h-10 w-px bg-gray-200 dark:bg-gray-700"></div>
      <a href="https://eit.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
        <img
          src={`${base}/images/EIT.png`}
          alt="Ellison Institute of Technology"
          class="h-10 object-contain"
        />
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Key dates strip -->
  <section class="grid sm:grid-cols-3 gap-4 mb-16">
    {[
      { label: 'Submission Deadline', date: 'September 2026' },
      { label: 'Author Notification', date: 'October 2026' },
      { label: 'Workshop Date',       date: 'December 2026' },
    ].map(({ label, date }) => (
      <div class="rounded-xl border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-800 bg-white dark:bg-gray-900 p-5 text-center shadow-sm">
        <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-gray-400 dark:text-gray-500 mb-1">{label}</p>
        <p class="text-base font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-gray-100">{date}</p>
      </div>
    ))}
  </section>

  <!-- Abstract -->
  <section class="mb-16">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-4">About the Workshop</h2>
    <div class="space-y-4 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300 leading-relaxed text-base">
      <p>
        Large language models (LLMs) are routinely adapted to downstream applications through
        post-training methods, such as instruction tuning and domain adaption. Yet in
        real-world deployment, downstream tasks rarely remain fixed: objectives shift, data
        distributions drift, feedback signals evolve, and evaluation standards change over time.
        Post-training therefore becomes a process of repeated adaptation in non-stationary
        environments. Despite its central role in modern foundation models, the theoretical
        foundations of this adaptive post-training paradigm remain limited. Current practices
        are largely heuristic, with incomplete understanding of statistical identifiability,
        optimization dynamics, robustness to misspecification, and trade-offs between adaptation
        and capability preservation. These gaps are particularly consequential in safety-critical
        settings, where unintended regressions or feedback loops may arise under evolving
        conditions. This workshop aims to develop principled foundations for LLM post-training
        under task evolution. We bring together researchers from machine learning theory,
        reinforcement learning, and AI safety to develop principled foundations for this.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Quick links -->
  <section class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
    {[
      { href: `${base}/call/`,       label: 'Call for Papers',      desc: 'Topics, submission guidelines, and key dates.' },
      { href: `${base}/program/`,    label: 'Workshop Program',     desc: 'Full schedule for the day.' },
      { href: `${base}/papers/`,     label: 'Accepted Papers',      desc: 'Browse the accepted submissions.' },
      { href: `${base}/organisers/`, label: 'Organising Committee', desc: 'Meet the team behind the workshop.' },
    ].map(({ href, label, desc }) => (
      <a href={href} class="flex flex-col rounded-xl border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-800 bg-white dark:bg-gray-900 p-5 hover:border-indigo-400 dark:hover:border-indigo-600 shadow-sm hover:shadow-md transition-all group">
        <span class="font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-gray-100 group-hover:text-indigo-600 dark:group-hover:text-indigo-400 transition-colors">{label} &rarr;</span>
        <span class="text-sm text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400 mt-1">{desc}</span>
      </a>
    ))}
  </section>
</Layout>
